From 4f85d4681c981d2ce2512e728af9d6a7dd63352c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:06:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: native WebSocket subscription limits

Port chronik-http's subscription_limits.rs: a SubscriptionLimiter shared
by every WebSocket session that caps the total number of subscriptions
(-chronikmaxsubs), the subscriptions per client IP (-chronikmaxsubsperip)
and the size of a subscribed script (-chroniksubsmaxscriptsize).
Exceeding a limit yields the same "503: ..." messages as Rust, duplicate
subscriptions don't take a slot, and a SubscriptionGuard releases its slot
when the subscription ends.

With the native in-process /chronik/ws, the per-IP limit keys on the real
client address instead of the proxy's loopback socket.

Tier: eCash

Coordinator integration provenance (metrics369):
Introduce optional atomic-only subscription reservation/release observer at first limiter consumer; contain observer exceptions and retain exact caps and guard lifetime; deferred causal control included.
All build/runtime/observer controls deferred by user compile-first policy; ordered source replay is not runtime approval.
